From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0157: flips return without waiting for the latch

backboardd waited ~7 ms of every frame for the DPU to latch its flip
(scrolling Settings: ~15 ms of drawing + 7 ms wait = ~45 fps). A flip now
returns after the flush. backboardd alternates two buffers, so its next
frame is drawn into the buffer still being fetched until the latch: GPU
work that writes an IOSurface waits for the pending latch first
(blue_dpu_flip_settle, from the submit), overlapping CoreAnimation's CPU
work for the frame. bluedpu_flip_sync=1 waits in the flip as before.
---
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/BlueDPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/BlueDPU.cpp
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@
